				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-5a6495a elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-theme-post-content" data-id="5a6495a" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="theme-post-content.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container" style="content-visibility: auto;contain-intrinsic-size: auto 28521px;">
					<div class="abh_box abh_box_up abh_box_business"><ul class="abh_tabs"> <li class="abh_about abh_active"><a href="#abh_about">About</a></li> <li class="abh_posts"><a href="#abh_posts">Latest Posts</a></li></ul><div class="abh_tab_content"><section class="vcard author abh_about_tab abh_tab" itemscope itemprop="author" itemtype="https://schema.org/Person" style="display:block"><div class="abh_image" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/ImageObject"><a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/author/sharonfirstaidpro-com-au/" class="url" title="Sharon McCulloch"> <img decoding="async" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/gravatar/sharon-mcculloch-2.jpg" class="photo" width="250" alt="Sharon McCulloch" height="250" loading="lazy" fetchpriority="low"></a> </div><div class="abh_social"> </div><div class="abh_text"><div class="abh_name fn name" itemprop="name"><a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/author/sharonfirstaidpro-com-au/" class="url">Sharon McCulloch</a></div><div class="abh_job"><span class="title">CEO, Founder and First Aid Trainer</span> at <span class="org"><a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/" target="_blank">FirstAidPro</a></span></div><div class="description note abh_description" itemprop="description">Sharon McCulloch is the CEO and Founder of FirstAidPro, Australia's leading Registered Training Organisation (31124), delivering First Aid Courses nationwide.<br><br>Sharon has 21+ years of experience as a qualified Emergency Care Nurse registered with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (APHRA) and 12+ years as a First Aid Trainer.<br><br>She takes pride in FirstAidPro making first aid training available, comprehensive and affordable to everybody.</div></div> </section><section class="abh_posts_tab abh_tab"><div class="abh_image"><a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/author/sharonfirstaidpro-com-au/" class="url" title="Sharon McCulloch"><img decoding="async" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/gravatar/sharon-mcculloch-2.jpg" class="photo" width="250" alt="Sharon McCulloch" height="250" loading="lazy" fetchpriority="low"></a></div><div class="abh_social"> </div><div class="abh_text"><div class="abh_name">Latest posts by Sharon McCulloch <span class="abh_allposts">(<a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/author/sharonfirstaidpro-com-au/">see all</a>)</span></div><div class="abh_description note"><ul>				<li>					<a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/blog/international-day-of-people-with-disability-2026/">International Day of People with Disability 2026: Building a Career in Disability Support</a><span> - 20/11/2026</span>				</li>				<li>					<a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/blog/f-first-aid-requirements-for-security-licence/">First Aid Requirements for Security Licence Holders in Australia</a><span> - 20/11/2026</span>				</li>				<li>					<a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/blog/national-water-safety-day-2026/">National Water Safety Day: Drowning First Aid Every Australian Should Know</a><span> - 19/11/2026</span>				</li></ul></div></div> </section></div> <div data-elementor-type="wp-post" data-elementor-id="1948662" class="elementor elementor-1948662" data-elementor-post-type="post">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-720ec2f8 e-flex e-con-boxed elementor-repeater-item-default_padding elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover e-con e-parent" data-id="720ec2f8" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container" data-settings='{"ang_container_spacing_size":"default_padding"}'>
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-541b5ec5 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="541b5ec5" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Pain management in <a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/course/hltaid011/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">first aid</a> involves systematic assessment and treatment techniques used by trained first aiders to reduce suffering and improve patient outcomes in workplace and community emergency situations. Effective pain relief in <a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/course/hltaid011/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">first aid</a> settings combines non-pharmacological methods like cold therapy, elevation, and immobilisation with appropriate medication administration, all while ensuring safety and recognising when to access professional medical help.</span></p><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Understanding how to manage pain effectively is crucial for anyone providing <a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/course/hltaid011/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">first aid</a>, whether in workplace environments, community settings, or emergency situations. The ability to recognise different types of pain, assess severity accurately, and apply suitable treatment methods can significantly improve a patient&rsquo;s quality of life during critical moments before professional medical care arrives.</span></p><p><b>Ready to advance your first aid skills?</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> First Aid Pro offers<a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/course/puaeme008/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"> nationally recognised PUAEME008 Provide Pain Management</a> courses across Australia. Our comprehensive training covers workplace safety requirements and advanced pain management techniques for first aiders.</span> <a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/course/puaeme008/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Register today</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> to enhance your emergency response capabilities.</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-2ef5d1cf external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="2ef5d1cf" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img fetchpriority="low" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="612" height="604" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Pain-Management-chart.jpg" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1948715" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Pain-Management-chart.jpg 612w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Pain-Management-chart-300x296.jpg 300w" sizes="auto" loading="lazy">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-4146a9a7 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="4146a9a7" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h3 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default" id="key-takeaways">Key Takeaways</h3>				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-4c97ad91 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="4c97ad91" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<ul><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Assessment First:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Always conduct systematic pain assessment using OPQRST before implementing any treatment strategies. Accurate assessment guides appropriate intervention and helps identify medical emergencies requiring immediate professional care.</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Non-Drug Options:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Cold therapy, elevation, compression, and immobilisation provide effective first-line pain management without medication risks. These techniques should be attempted before or alongside pharmacological interventions.</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Medication Safety:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Understand paracetamol vs ibuprofen indications, contraindications, and proper dosing guidelines. Always check for allergies, existing medical conditions, and potential drug interactions before administration.</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Know Your Scope:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Recognise when pain requires emergency services (000) or advanced medical care. Red flag symptoms include altered consciousness, signs of shock, or severe pain unresponsive to basic interventions.</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Document Everything:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Maintain detailed records of pain scores, treatments administered, and patient responses. Proper documentation ensures continuity of care and protects both patient and provider.</span></li></ul>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-b3aff39 external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="b3aff39" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img decoding="async" width="800" height="469" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/OPQRST.webp" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1948733" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/OPQRST.webp 800w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/OPQRST-300x176.webp 300w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/OPQRST-768x450.webp 768w" sizes="auto" loading="lazy" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-5f35d1e3 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="5f35d1e3" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h2 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default" id="when-pain-management-in-first-aid-is-necessary">When Pain Management in First Aid is Necessary</h2>				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-644e7696 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="644e7696" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<h3 id="using-opqrst-and-pain-assessment-scales"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Using OPQRST and Pain Assessment Scales</span></h3><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Proper pain assessment forms the foundation of effective pain management in <a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/course/hltaid011/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">first aid</a>. Before administering any treatment, first aiders must systematically evaluate the patient&rsquo;s condition to ensure appropriate care and identify potential medical emergencies requiring immediate ambulance assistance.</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-a39bc98 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="a39bc98" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<!-- OPQRST Pain Assessment Technique &ndash; Elementor/WordPress HTML Widget -->
<div class="opqrst-infographic" role="group" aria-label="OPQRST Pain Assessment Technique">
  <style>.opqrst-infographic {
      --bg: #FFFFFF;
      --row-a: #E4EAE4;   /* soft grey-green */
      --row-b: #DDEBE9;   /* soft mint/cyan */
      --text: #16231F;    /* very dark green */
      --head: #20342E;    /* dark green */
      --accent: #116914;  /* bright green */
      --alert: #BC0000;   /* bright red */
      --muted: #3A3A3A;   /* dark grey */
      --blue: #4682B4;    /* steel blue (brand ref) */
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Arial, sans-serif;
      color: var(--text);
      background: var(--bg);
      border: 1px solid #d6e2d6;
      border-radius: 18px;
      box-shadow: 0 6px 18px rgba(22,35,31,0.08);
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .opqrst-header {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--head), #16231F);
      color: #FFFFFF;
      padding: 22px 24px;
      border-bottom: 4px solid var(--accent);
    }
    .opqrst-header h2 {
      margin: 0 0 6px 0;
      font-size: 1.4rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.2px;
    }
    .opqrst-header p {
      margin: 0;
      opacity: 0.9;
      font-size: 0.98rem;
    }

    .opqrst-table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      table-layout: fixed;
    }
    .opqrst-table thead th {
      background: #f4f7f4;
      color: var(--head);
      text-align: left;
      padding: 14px 16px;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #dfe8df;
    }
    .opqrst-table tbody tr:nth-child(odd) { background: var(--row-a); }
    .opqrst-table tbody tr:nth-child(even){ background: var(--row-b); }
    .opqrst-table td {
      padding: 14px 16px;
      vertical-align: top;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(32,52,46,0.06);
      font-size: 0.98rem;
      line-height: 1.4;
    }

    /* Component cell with letter chip */
    .opqrst-component {
      display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;
      font-weight: 700; color: var(--head);
    }
    .opqrst-chip {
      display: inline-grid; place-items: center;
      width: 36px; height: 36px; border-radius: 999px;
      font-weight: 800; color: #FFFFFF;
      box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(255,255,255,0.12), 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.12);
      letter-spacing: 0.5px;
      flex: 0 0 36px;
    }
    .chip-o { background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), #0e5a10); }
    .chip-p { background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--head), #0f1c18); }
    .chip-q { background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--blue), #315e80); }
    .chip-r { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #006737, #024c29); }
    .chip-s { background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--alert), #8f0000); }
    .chip-t { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #116914, #0c4d10); }

    /* Small badges */
    .opqrst-badge {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 2px 8px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      background: #ffffe0; /* #FFFFE0 from brand set */
      color: var(--head);
      border: 1px solid rgba(32,52,46,0.15);
    }

    /* Footnote */
    .opqrst-foot {
      padding: 14px 16px 18px 16px;
      background: #f8fbf8;
      border-top: 1px dashed #d6e2d6;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }
    .opqrst-foot strong { color: var(--head); }

    /* Accessibility & hover niceties on desktop */
    @media (hover:hover) {
      .opqrst-table tbody tr:hover { filter: brightness(0.98); }
    }

    /* Mobile: convert table rows into cards with labels */
    @media (max-width: 800px) {
      .opqrst-table thead { display: none; }
      .opqrst-table, .opqrst-table tbody, .opqrst-table tr, .opqrst-table td { display: block; width: 100%; }
      .opqrst-table tr {
        margin: 10px 12px;
        border: 1px solid #d6e2d6;
        border-radius: 14px;
        overflow: hidden;
        box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(22,35,31,0.06);
      }
      .opqrst-table td {
        border: 0;
        padding: 12px 14px;
        position: relative;
      }
      .opqrst-table td::before {
        content: attr(data-label);
        display: block;
        font-size: 0.78rem;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        color: var(--muted);
        margin-bottom: 6px;
        opacity: 0.9;
      }
      .opqrst-component { margin-top: 4px; }
    }</style>

  <div class="opqrst-header">
    <h2 id="opqrst-pain-assessment-technique">OPQRST Pain Assessment Technique</h2>
    <p>Use this structured approach to explore a patient&rsquo;s pain history to guide safe, effective first aid.</p>
  </div>

  <table class="opqrst-table" role="table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Component</th>
        <th scope="col">Questions to Ask</th>
        <th scope="col">Why It Matters</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td class="opqrst-component" data-label="Component">
          <span class="opqrst-chip chip-o" aria-hidden="true">O</span> <span>Onset</span>
        </td>
        <td data-label="Questions to Ask">When did the pain start? Was it sudden or gradual?</td>
        <td data-label="Why It Matters">Helps identify acute vs chronic conditions</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td class="opqrst-component" data-label="Component">
          <span class="opqrst-chip chip-p" aria-hidden="true">P</span> <span>Provocation</span>
        </td>
        <td data-label="Questions to Ask">What makes it better or worse?</td>
        <td data-label="Why It Matters">Guides treatment decisions</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td class="opqrst-component" data-label="Component">
          <span class="opqrst-chip chip-q" aria-hidden="true">Q</span> <span>Quality</span>
        </td>
        <td data-label="Questions to Ask">How would you describe the pain? <span class="opqrst-badge">sharp</span> <span class="opqrst-badge">dull</span> <span class="opqrst-badge">burning</span></td>
        <td data-label="Why It Matters">Indicates potential injury type</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td class="opqrst-component" data-label="Component">
          <span class="opqrst-chip chip-r" aria-hidden="true">R</span> <span>Radiation</span>
        </td>
        <td data-label="Questions to Ask">Does the pain spread anywhere else?</td>
        <td data-label="Why It Matters">May reveal serious underlying conditions</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td class="opqrst-component" data-label="Component">
          <span class="opqrst-chip chip-s" aria-hidden="true">S</span> <span>Severity</span>
        </td>
        <td data-label="Questions to Ask">Rate your pain from <strong>0&ndash;10</strong>.</td>
        <td data-label="Why It Matters">Determines urgency and treatment approach</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td class="opqrst-component" data-label="Component">
          <span class="opqrst-chip chip-t" aria-hidden="true">T</span> <span>Timing</span>
        </td>
        <td data-label="Questions to Ask">Is it constant or intermittent?</td>
        <td data-label="Why It Matters">Affects medication timing and effectiveness</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="opqrst-foot">
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> For <em>Severity</em>, use the <strong>0&ndash;10</strong> numeric rating scale (0 = no pain, 10 = worst imaginable). Reassess after interventions (e.g., rest, ice, immobilisation) to monitor change.</p>
  </div>
</div>
				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-bc0e3c4 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="bc0e3c4" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">This systematic assessment helps first aiders make informed decisions about treatment while providing valuable information to paramedics and medical professionals during handover.</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-d8f2397 external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="d8f2397" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img decoding="async" width="612" height="367" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Pain-scale.jpg" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1948765" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Pain-scale.jpg 612w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/Pain-scale-300x180.jpg.webp 300w" sizes="auto" loading="lazy" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-c338ab4 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="c338ab4" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<h3 id="pain-scale-0-10-first-aid-applications"><b>Pain Scale 0&ndash;10 First Aid Applications</b></h3><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The numeric rating scale is the most widely used pain assessment tool in <a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/course/hltaid011/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">first aid</a> situations. Patients rate their pain from 0 (no pain) to 10 (worst imaginable pain), providing a standardised measure that healthcare professionals can track over time.</span></p><p><b>Pain Scale Guidelines:</b></p><ul><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>0-3:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Mild pain &ndash; usually manageable with basic first aid techniques</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>4-6:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Moderate pain &ndash; may require medication and non-pharmacological interventions</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>7-10:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Severe pain &ndash; often requires emergency medical attention and advanced pain management</span></li></ul><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">For unconscious patients or those unable to communicate, first aiders should observe behavioural indicators including facial expressions, body positioning, vital signs changes, and vocal responses to assess pain levels.</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-28a6870b external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="28a6870b" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="800" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/cold-pack.webp" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1948779" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/cold-pack.webp 800w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/cold-pack-300x300.webp 300w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/cold-pack-150x150.webp 150w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/cold-pack-768x768.webp 768w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/cold-pack-400x400.webp 400w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/cold-pack-650x650.webp 650w" sizes="auto" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-5cb405c6 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="5cb405c6" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h2 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default" id="non-pharmacological-pain-relief-first-aid-techniques">Non-Pharmacological Pain Relief First Aid Techniques
</h2>				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-e1d7101 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="e1d7101" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Many effective pain management strategies don&rsquo;t involve medication, making them ideal for workplace <a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/course/hltaid011/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">first aid</a> situations where drug administration may be restricted or inappropriate. These techniques can provide immediate relief while reducing the risk of complications.</span></p><h3 id="cold-pack-for-pain-first-aid-management"><b>Cold Pack for Pain First Aid Management</b></h3><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Cold therapy remains one of the most effective non-pharmacological pain relief methods available to first aiders. Proper application can significantly reduce pain, swelling, and inflammation in acute injuries.</span></p><p><b>Cold Therapy Application:</b></p><ul><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Apply within the first 15-20 minutes after injury</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Use commercial cold packs or ice wrapped in a thin towel</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Apply for 15-20 minutes every 2-3 hours for first 24-48 hours</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Never apply ice directly to skin to prevent frostbite</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Check circulation regularly during application</span></li></ul><p><b>When to Use Cold vs Heat:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Cold therapy is appropriate for acute injuries, inflammation, and swelling. Heat therapy should only be used for chronic muscle tension or after the acute inflammatory phase (usually after 48-72 hours). Ensure you consult appropriate medical advice when uncertain.</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-23ddcc7e external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="23ddcc7e" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="557" height="466" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RICER-first-aid-for-sprains-strains-and-fractures-PIP-7-1.gif" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1948790" alt="" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-2477c46a elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="2477c46a" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<h3 id="elevation-to-reduce-pain-and-swelling"><b>Elevation to Reduce Pain and Swelling</b></h3><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Elevating an injured limb above the level of the heart uses gravity to reduce blood flow to the injury site, thereby decreasing swelling and associated pain. This technique works particularly well for extremity injuries and should be combined with other pain management strategies.</span></p><p><b>Proper Elevation Technique:</b></p><ol><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Position the injured area above heart level when possible</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Support the limb comfortably using pillows or soft materials</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Ensure circulation isn&rsquo;t compromised</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Monitor for changes in colour, temperature, or sensation</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Maintain elevation for extended periods when practical</span></li></ol>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-63732c10 external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="63732c10" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="534" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/compression-bandage.webp" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1948802" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/compression-bandage.webp 800w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/compression-bandage-300x200.webp 300w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/compression-bandage-768x513.webp 768w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/compression-bandage-600x400.webp 600w" sizes="auto" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-4a7ed0fe elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="4a7ed0fe" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<h3 id="compression-bandage-for-pain-control"><b>Compression Bandage for Pain Control</b></h3><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Appropriate compression can reduce swelling, provide support to injured tissues, and subsequently decrease pain levels. However, improper technique can compromise circulation and worsen the patient&rsquo;s condition.</span></p><p><b>Compression Guidelines:</b></p><ul><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Apply firm, even pressure without restricting blood flow</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Use appropriate bandage width for the injury site</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Start distal (furthest from heart) and work proximally</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Check circulation every 15-20 minutes</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Look for signs of compromised blood flow: blue/grey skin colour, coldness, numbness</span></li></ul>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-3cc902fa external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="3cc902fa" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="534" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/splinting-for-immobilation.webp" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1948806" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/splinting-for-immobilation.webp 800w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/splinting-for-immobilation-300x200.webp 300w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/splinting-for-immobilation-768x513.webp 768w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/splinting-for-immobilation-600x400.webp 600w" sizes="auto" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-4c9bdaf7 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="4c9bdaf7" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<h3 id="immobilisation-first-aid-splinting-for-pain-relief"><b>Immobilisation First Aid: Splinting for Pain Relief</b></h3><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Immobilising injured areas prevents further damage and significantly reduces pain by limiting movement. This technique is particularly effective for suspected fractures, severe sprains, and joint injuries.</span></p><p><b>Basic Splinting Principles:</b></p><ul><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Splint above and below the injury site</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Use rigid materials when available (boards, magazines, rolled newspapers)</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Pad bony prominences to prevent pressure sores</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Secure firmly but allow for swelling</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Check circulation, sensation, and movement regularly</span></li></ul><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">For upper limb injuries, slings provide excellent support while allowing some mobility. Ensure the sling supports the weight of the arm without putting excessive pressure on the neck.</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-b1b79f9 external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="b1b79f9" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="454" height="340" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/pain-strategies.jpeg" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1948791" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/pain-strategies.jpeg 454w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/pain-strategies-300x225.jpeg.webp 300w" sizes="auto" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-2f7511fe elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="2f7511fe" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<h2 id="rice-vs-peace-love-soft-tissue-injuries-protocol"><b>RICE vs PEACE &amp; LOVE Soft-Tissue Injuries Protocol</b></h2><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Understanding both traditional and modern approaches to soft-tissue injury management ensures first aiders can apply the most appropriate and evidence-based techniques for optimal patient outcomes.</span></p><h3 id="traditional-ricer-first-aid-method"><b>Traditional RICER First Aid Method</b></h3><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The RICER protocol has been widely taught in <a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/course/hltaid011/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">first aid training</a> for decades and remains relevant for immediate injury management:</span></p><ul><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Rest:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Cease activity to prevent further injury</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Ice:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Apply cold therapy to reduce inflammation</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Compression:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Apply appropriate pressure to limit swelling</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Elevation:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Raise injured area above heart level</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Referral:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Seek appropriate medical assessment</span></li></ul><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">While RICER remains effective for immediate injury management, recent studies suggest that prolonged rest may actually impede recovery in some cases.</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-e657847 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="e657847" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<!-- PEACE & LOVE &ndash; Soft-Tissue Injury Care | Elementor/WordPress HTML Widget -->
<div class="peace-love-infographic" role="group" aria-label="PEACE &amp; LOVE soft-tissue injury care">
  <style>.peace-love-infographic{
      --bg:#FFFFFF;
      --row-a:#E4EAE4;          /* soft grey-green */
      --row-b:#DDEBE9;          /* soft mint/cyan */
      --text:#16231F;           /* very dark green */
      --head:#20342E;           /* dark green */
      --accent:#116914;         /* bright green */
      --alert:#BC0000;          /* bright red */
      --muted:#3A3A3A;          /* dark grey */
      --pale:#FFFFE0;           /* soft highlight */
      --steel:#4682B4;          /* steel blue (brand ref) */
      color:var(--text);
      background:var(--bg);
      border:1px solid #d6e2d6;
      border-radius:18px;
      box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(22,35,31,0.08);
      overflow:hidden;
      font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Roboto,Arial,sans-serif;
    }

    /* Header */
    .pl-header{
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--head),#16231F);
      color:#fff;
      padding:22px 24px;
      border-bottom:4px solid var(--accent);
    }
    .pl-header h2{
      margin:0 0 6px 0;
      font-size:1.4rem;
      letter-spacing:.2px;
    }
    .pl-header p{
      margin:0;
      opacity:.95;
      font-size:.98rem;
    }

    /* Panels */
    .pl-grid{
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;
      gap:18px;
      padding:18px;
    }
    .pl-panel{
      background:#f8fbf8;
      border:1px solid #d6e2d6;
      border-radius:14px;
      overflow:hidden;
      box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(22,35,31,0.06);
    }
    .pl-panel h3{
      margin:0;
      padding:14px 16px;
      font-size:1.05rem;
      color:#fff;
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--steel),#315e80);
      border-bottom:2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);
    }
    .pl-panel.peace h3{
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--accent),#0e5a10);
    }
    .pl-panel .pl-steps{
      margin:0;
      padding:0;
      list-style:none;
    }

    /* Steps */
    .pl-step{
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;
      gap:12px;
      padding:14px 16px;
      border-bottom:1px solid rgba(32,52,46,0.06);
    }
    .pl-step:nth-child(odd){ background:var(--row-a); }
    .pl-step:nth-child(even){ background:var(--row-b); }

    .pl-chip{
      display:inline-grid;
      place-items:center;
      width:38px;height:38px;
      border-radius:999px;
      color:#fff;
      font-weight:800;
      letter-spacing:.5px;
      box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(255,255,255,0.12),0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.12);
      user-select:none;
    }
    .chip-P,.chip-L{ background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--head),#0f1c18); }
    .chip-E,.chip-O{ background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--steel),#315e80); }
    .chip-A,.chip-V{ background:linear-gradient(135deg,#006737,#024c29); }
    .chip-C,.chip-E2{ background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--accent),#0c4d10); }

    .pl-title{
      font-weight:800;
      color:var(--head);
      margin:0 0 4px 0;
      display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px;
    }
    .pl-desc{ margin:0; font-size:.98rem; line-height:1.45; }

    /* Badges */
    .pl-badge{
      display:inline-block;
      padding:2px 8px;
      border-radius:999px;
      font-size:.82rem;
      font-weight:700;
      background:var(--pale);
      color:var(--head);
      border:1px solid rgba(32,52,46,0.15);
    }
    .pl-badge.alert{
      background:rgba(188,0,0,0.08);
      color:var(--alert);
      border-color:rgba(188,0,0,0.25);
    }

    /* Footnote */
    .pl-foot{
      padding:14px 16px 18px 16px;
      background:#f4f7f4;
      border-top:1px dashed #d6e2d6;
      font-size:.95rem;
    }
    .pl-foot strong{ color:var(--head); }

    /* Hover on desktop */
    @media (hover:hover){
      .pl-step:hover{ filter:brightness(.98); }
    }

    /* Mobile */
    @media (max-width:900px){
      .pl-grid{ grid-template-columns:1fr; }
    }</style>

  <div class="pl-header">
    <h2 id="modern-peace-love-approach">Modern <span style="font-weight:900;">PEACE &amp; LOVE</span> Approach</h2>
    <p>Current best practice for soft-tissue injury care&mdash;immediate steps (PEACE) followed by active recovery (LOVE).</p>
  </div>

  <div class="pl-grid">
    <!-- PEACE Panel -->
    <section class="pl-panel peace" aria-label="PEACE &ndash; Immediate Care">
      <h3 id="peace-immediate-care">PEACE (Immediate Care)</h3>
      <ul class="pl-steps">
        <li class="pl-step">
          <span class="pl-chip chip-P" aria-hidden="true">P</span>
          <div>
            <p class="pl-title">Protect</p>
            <p class="pl-desc">Unload or restrict movement for <strong>1&ndash;3 days</strong> to limit aggravation.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="pl-step">
          <span class="pl-chip chip-E" aria-hidden="true">E</span>
          <div>
            <p class="pl-title">Elevate</p>
            <p class="pl-desc">Elevate the limb <em>above heart level</em> to help reduce swelling.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="pl-step">
          <span class="pl-chip chip-A" aria-hidden="true">A</span>
          <div>
            <p class="pl-title">Avoid Anti-inflammatories <span class="pl-badge alert">Caution</span></p>
            <p class="pl-desc">They may <strong>impair tissue healing</strong> in the early phase; seek clinical advice before use.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="pl-step">
          <span class="pl-chip chip-C" aria-hidden="true">C</span>
          <div>
            <p class="pl-title">Compress</p>
            <p class="pl-desc">Apply external mechanical pressure (e.g., elastic bandage) to limit oedema and pain.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="pl-step">
          <span class="pl-chip chip-E" aria-hidden="true">E</span>
          <div>
            <p class="pl-title">Educate</p>
            <p class="pl-desc">Explain the condition, expected recovery, and self-management strategies to support informed choices.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- LOVE Panel -->
    <section class="pl-panel love" aria-label="LOVE &ndash; Ongoing Management">
      <h3 id="love-ongoing-management">LOVE (Ongoing Management)</h3>
      <ul class="pl-steps">
        <li class="pl-step">
          <span class="pl-chip chip-L" aria-hidden="true">L</span>
          <div>
            <p class="pl-title">Load</p>
            <p class="pl-desc">Gradually return to normal activities as symptoms allow; use pain as a guide.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="pl-step">
          <span class="pl-chip chip-O" aria-hidden="true">O</span>
          <div>
            <p class="pl-title">Optimism</p>
            <p class="pl-desc">A positive outlook is associated with <strong>better outcomes</strong> and adherence to rehab.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="pl-step">
          <span class="pl-chip chip-V" aria-hidden="true">V</span>
          <div>
            <p class="pl-title">Vascularisation</p>
            <p class="pl-desc">Introduce <strong>pain-free cardiovascular activity</strong> early to promote healing.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="pl-step">
          <span class="pl-chip chip-E2" aria-hidden="true">E</span>
          <div>
            <p class="pl-title">Exercise</p>
            <p class="pl-desc">Progress mobility, strength, and functional exercises to restore full capacity.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="pl-foot">
    <p><strong>Notes:</strong> Protect briefly&mdash;then reintroduce <em>symptom-guided</em> loading. Seek medical care for severe pain, deformity, or red-flag symptoms. In an emergency, call <strong>000</strong>.</p>
  </div>
</div>
				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-04e5b7e elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="04e5b7e" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">This approach emphasises active recovery while respecting the natural healing process, leading to better long-term outcomes for many patients.</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-7cc9b8d external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="7cc9b8d" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="2000" height="1414" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/Ibuprofen-vs-Paracetamol-1.png.webp" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1948855" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/Ibuprofen-vs-Paracetamol-1.png.webp 2000w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/Ibuprofen-vs-Paracetamol-1-300x212.png.webp 300w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/Ibuprofen-vs-Paracetamol-1-1024x724.png.webp 1024w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/Ibuprofen-vs-Paracetamol-1-768x543.png.webp 768w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/Ibuprofen-vs-Paracetamol-1-1536x1086.png.webp 1536w" sizes="auto" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-5c27eca elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="5c27eca" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h2 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default" id="paracetamol-vs-ibuprofen-australian-first-aid-guidelines">Paracetamol vs Ibuprofen: Australian First Aid Guidelines</h2>				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-60ef426 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="60ef426" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">First aiders in workplace and community settings often need to decide between different over-the-counter pain medications. Understanding the differences between paracetamol and ibuprofen ensures safe and effective treatment while reducing the risk of adverse reactions.</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-9453682 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="9453682" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<!-- Paracetamol First Aid Applications (responsive, unsquashable) -->
<div class="para-infographic v2" role="group" aria-label="Paracetamol First Aid Applications">
  <style>.para-infographic.v2{
      /* Brand palette */
      --bg:#FFFFFF;
      --row-a:#E4EAE4;
      --row-b:#DDEBE9;
      --text:#16231F;
      --head:#20342E;
      --accent:#116914;
      --alert:#BC0000;
      --muted:#3A3A3A;
      --pale:#FFFFE0;
      --steel:#4682B4;

      /* Layout guards (tweak these if needed) */
      --col-min: 420px;   /* min width for each main column */
      --dose-min: 320px;  /* min width for each dosing card */

      color:var(--text);
      background:var(--bg);
      border:1px solid #d6e2d6;
      border-radius:18px;
      box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(22,35,31,0.08);
      overflow:hidden;
      font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Roboto,Arial,sans-serif;
    }

    /* Header */
    .para-header{
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--head),#16231F);
      color:#fff;
      padding:22px 24px;
      border-bottom:4px solid var(--accent);
    }
    .para-header h2{ margin:0 0 6px 0; font-size:1.4rem; letter-spacing:.2px; }
    .para-header p{ margin:0; opacity:.95; font-size:.98rem; }

    /* Main grid: columns only appear if each can be >= --col-min */
    .para-grid{
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(var(--col-min), 1fr));
      gap:18px;
      padding:18px;
    }
    .para-panel{
      background:#f8fbf8;
      border:1px solid #d6e2d6;
      border-radius:14px;
      overflow:hidden;
      box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(22,35,31,0.06);
      min-width:0; /* prevents content from forcing panel wider than its grid track */
    }
    .para-panel h3{
      margin:0;
      padding:14px 16px;
      font-size:1.05rem;
      color:#fff;
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--steel),#315e80);
      border-bottom:2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);
    }
    .para-panel.advantages h3{
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--accent),#0e5a10);
    }

    /* Advantages list */
    .para-list{ margin:0; padding:0; list-style:none; }
    .para-item{
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;
      gap:12px;
      padding:14px 16px;
      border-bottom:1px solid rgba(32,52,46,0.06);
    }
    .para-item:nth-child(odd){ background:var(--row-a); }
    .para-item:nth-child(even){ background:var(--row-b); }

    .para-chip{
      display:inline-grid; place-items:center;
      width:38px; height:38px; border-radius:999px;
      color:#fff; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:.5px;
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--head),#0f1c18);
      box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(255,255,255,0.12),0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.12);
      user-select:none;
      flex:0 0 38px;
    }
    .para-title{ margin:0 0 4px 0; font-weight:800; color:var(--head); }
    .para-desc{ margin:0; font-size:.98rem; line-height:1.45; word-break:normal; }

    /* Dosing section */
    .dose-wrap{ padding:10px 12px 16px; }
    .dose-grid{
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(var(--dose-min), 1fr));
      gap:12px;
    }
    .dose-card{
      background:#fff;
      border:1px solid #d6e2d6;
      border-radius:12px;
      padding:12px;
      box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(22,35,31,0.05);
      min-width:0; /* important to allow shrink inside grid track */
    }
    .dose-card h4{ margin:0 0 8px 0; font-size:1rem; color:var(--head); }

    .dose-table{
      width:100%;
      border-collapse:collapse;
      table-layout:fixed;
      font-size:.96rem;
    }
    .dose-table th,.dose-table td{
      text-align:left; padding:8px 10px;
      border-bottom:1px solid rgba(32,52,46,0.08);
      vertical-align:top;
      word-wrap:break-word;
    }
    .dose-table thead th{ background:#f4f7f4; color:var(--head); font-weight:700; }

    .badge{
      display:inline-block; padding:2px 8px; border-radius:999px;
      font-size:.82rem; font-weight:700; background:var(--pale); color:var(--head);
      border:1px solid rgba(32,52,46,0.15); margin-left:6px;
    }
    .badge.alert{
      background:rgba(188,0,0,0.08); color:var(--alert); border-color:rgba(188,0,0,0.25);
    }

    .para-foot{
      padding:14px 16px 18px 16px;
      background:#f4f7f4; border-top:1px dashed #d6e2d6; font-size:.95rem;
    }
    .para-foot strong{ color:var(--head); }

    /* Table becomes card-like on very small screens */
    @media (max-width:520px){
      .dose-table thead{ display:none; }
      .dose-table, .dose-table tbody, .dose-table tr, .dose-table td{ display:block; width:100%; }
      .dose-table tr{ background:linear-gradient(0deg,var(--row-b),var(--row-a)); margin-bottom:10px; border:1px solid #d6e2d6; border-radius:10px; overflow:hidden; }
      .dose-table td{ border:0; padding:10px 12px; }
      .dose-table td::before{
        content:attr(data-label);
        display:block; font-size:.78rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.08em;
        color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:4px; opacity:.9;
      }
    }

    /* Subtle hover for desktop */
    @media (hover:hover){ .para-item:hover,.dose-card:hover{ filter:brightness(.98); } }</style>

  <div class="para-header">
    <h2 id="paracetamol-first-aid-applications">Paracetamol First Aid Applications</h2>
    <p>First-line option for mild&ndash;moderate pain in many first-aid situations due to a strong safety profile and broad effectiveness.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="para-grid">
    <!-- Advantages -->
    <section class="para-panel advantages" aria-label="Paracetamol Advantages">
      <h3 id="paracetamol-advantages">Paracetamol Advantages</h3>
      <ul class="para-list">
        <li class="para-item">
          <span class="para-chip" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
          <div>
            <p class="para-title">Suitable for most age groups</p>
            <p class="para-desc">From <strong>1 month</strong> of age with appropriate dosing and formulation.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="para-item">
          <span class="para-chip" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
          <div>
            <p class="para-title">Fewer drug interactions</p>
            <p class="para-desc">Generally fewer interactions than many other analgesics.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="para-item">
          <span class="para-chip" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
          <div>
            <p class="para-title">Compatible with many conditions</p>
            <p class="para-desc">Often suitable alongside common medical conditions (check individual advice).</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="para-item">
          <span class="para-chip" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
          <div>
            <p class="para-title">Effective for common pains</p>
            <p class="para-desc">Headaches, muscle pain, and general discomfort.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="para-item">
          <span class="para-chip" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
          <div>
            <p class="para-title">Multiple formulations</p>
            <p class="para-desc">Tablets, liquid, and suppositories to suit age and circumstance.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Dosing -->
    <section class="para-panel dosing" aria-label="Dosing Guidelines">
      <h3 id="dosing-guidelines">Dosing Guidelines</h3>
      <div class="dose-wrap">
        <div class="dose-grid">
          <div class="dose-card" role="region" aria-label="Adult dosing">
            <h4 id="adults-max-4000-mg-24-h">Adults <span class="badge">Max 4,000&nbsp;mg / 24&nbsp;h</span></h4>
            <table class="dose-table" role="table" aria-label="Adult dosing table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Dose</th>
                  <th scope="col">Frequency</th>
                  <th scope="col">Daily Maximum</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td data-label="Dose"><strong>500&ndash;1,000&nbsp;mg</strong></td>
                  <td data-label="Frequency">Every <strong>4&ndash;6 hours</strong></td>
                  <td data-label="Daily Maximum"><strong>4,000&nbsp;mg</strong> (24 hours)</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <div class="dose-card" role="region" aria-label="Children dosing">
            <h4 id="children-weight-based-max-60-mg-kg-24-h">Children <span class="badge">Weight-based</span> <span class="badge">Max 60&nbsp;mg/kg / 24&nbsp;h</span></h4>
            <table class="dose-table" role="table" aria-label="Children dosing table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Dose</th>
                  <th scope="col">Frequency</th>
                  <th scope="col">Daily Maximum</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td data-label="Dose"><strong>10&ndash;15&nbsp;mg/kg</strong> per dose</td>
                  <td data-label="Frequency">Every <strong>4&ndash;6 hours</strong></td>
                  <td data-label="Daily Maximum"><strong>60&nbsp;mg/kg</strong> (24 hours)</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="para-desc" style="margin:12px 4px 0;">
          <span class="badge">Important</span>
          Always check the medication packaging for specific instructions and formulation strength.
          <span class="badge alert">Safety</span>
          Never exceed the recommended daily maximums to prevent <strong>liver damage</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="para-foot">
    <p><strong>Notes:</strong> Paracetamol is called <em>acetaminophen</em> in some countries. Follow label directions and seek pharmacist/GP advice if unsure, for infants, pregnancy, liver disease, or if pain persists. In an emergency, call <strong>000</strong>.</p>
  </div>
</div>
				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-0e9bb3a elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="0e9bb3a" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p><b>Enhance your pain management expertise:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> First Aid Pro&rsquo;s <a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/course/puaeme008/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PUAEME008 course</a> covers advanced medication administration techniques for qualified first aiders. Learn about restricted analgesics, proper documentation, and workplace safety requirements.</span> <a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/course/puaeme008/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Enrol now</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> to expand your first aid capabilities.</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-4733b61 external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="4733b61" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="2560" height="1707" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/two-blister-packs-contains-black-and-white-pills-o-2025-02-11-23-41-52-utc-scaled.jpg" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1948864" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/two-blister-packs-contains-black-and-white-pills-o-2025-02-11-23-41-52-utc-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/two-blister-packs-contains-black-and-white-pills-o-2025-02-11-23-41-52-utc-300x200.jpg 300w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/two-blister-packs-contains-black-and-white-pills-o-2025-02-11-23-41-52-utc-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/two-blister-packs-contains-black-and-white-pills-o-2025-02-11-23-41-52-utc-768x512.jpg 768w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/two-blister-packs-contains-black-and-white-pills-o-2025-02-11-23-41-52-utc-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/two-blister-packs-contains-black-and-white-pills-o-2025-02-11-23-41-52-utc-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/two-blister-packs-contains-black-and-white-pills-o-2025-02-11-23-41-52-utc-600x400.jpg 600w" sizes="auto" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-594ba7f elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="594ba7f" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<h3 id="ibuprofen-first-aid-use-and-precautions"><b>Ibuprofen First Aid Use and Precautions</b></h3><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Ibuprofen belongs to the non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) class and offers both pain relief and anti-inflammatory effects, making it particularly useful for injuries involving inflammation.</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-4b1704f external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="4b1704f" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="732" height="509" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/When-Ibuprofen-is-Preferred_-visual-selection.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1948917" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/When-Ibuprofen-is-Preferred_-visual-selection.png 732w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/When-Ibuprofen-is-Preferred_-visual-selection-300x209.png.webp 300w" sizes="auto" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-e43e529 external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="e43e529" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="834" height="888" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Important-Contraindications-When-NOT-to-Give-Ibuprofen_-visual-selection-1.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1948922" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Important-Contraindications-When-NOT-to-Give-Ibuprofen_-visual-selection-1.png 834w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/Important-Contraindications-When-NOT-to-Give-Ibuprofen_-visual-selection-1-282x300.png.webp 282w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/Important-Contraindications-When-NOT-to-Give-Ibuprofen_-visual-selection-1-768x818.png.webp 768w" sizes="auto" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-65bbd45 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="65bbd45" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<h4 id="dosage-summary-table"><strong>Dosage Summary Table</strong></h4><table><tbody><tr><td><p><b>Medication</b></p></td><td><p><b>Adults</b></p></td><td><p><b>Children (6+ months)</b></p></td><td><p><b>Maximum Daily Dose</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Paracetamol</b></p></td><td><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">500-1000mg every 4-6 hours</span></p></td><td><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">10-15mg/kg every 4-6 hours</span></p></td><td><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Adults: 4000mg&lt;br&gt;Children: 60mg/kg</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Ibuprofen</b></p></td><td><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">200-400mg every 6-8 hours</span></p></td><td><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">5-10mg/kg every 6-8 hours</span></p></td><td><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Adults: 1200mg&lt;br&gt;Children: 30mg/kg</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-6620290 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="6620290" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<h3 id="children-pain-relief-first-aid-considerations"><b>Children Pain Relief First Aid Considerations</b></h3><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Administering pain medication to children requires special attention to dosing, consent, and age-appropriate techniques. Always seek parental consent when possible and maintain detailed records of any medication given.</span></p><p><b>Paediatric Pain Management Considerations:</b></p><ul><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Weight-based dosing is more accurate than age-based dosing</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Liquid formulations often preferred for children under 12</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Consider non-pharmacological methods first</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Monitor closely for adverse reactions</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Ensure medications are specifically formulated for children</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Never give adult-strength medications to children</span></li></ul>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-7487f0d elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="7487f0d" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h2 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default" id="pain-management-in-first-aid-for-specific-injuries">Pain Management in First Aid for Specific Injuries</h2>				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-aa03b5e elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="aa03b5e" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Different types of injuries require tailored approaches to pain management. Understanding how to modify techniques based on injury type ensures optimal patient comfort and outcomes.</span></p><h3 id="pain-management-in-first-aid-for-sprains-and-strains">Pain Management in First Aid for Sprains and Strains</h3><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Soft tissue injuries are among the most common workplace and sporting injuries requiring <a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/course/hltaid014/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">first aid</a> intervention. Effective pain management in first aid can prevent complications and promote faster recovery.</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-5b305f7 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="5b305f7" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<!-- Acute Management Strategy & Emergency Warning Signs | Elementor/WordPress HTML Widget -->
<div class="acute-infographic" role="group" aria-label="Acute Management Strategy and Emergency Warning Signs">
  <style>.acute-infographic{
      /* Brand palette (same as above) */
      --bg:#FFFFFF;
      --row-a:#E4EAE4;   /* soft grey-green */
      --row-b:#DDEBE9;   /* soft mint/cyan */
      --text:#16231F;    /* very dark green */
      --head:#20342E;    /* dark green */
      --accent:#116914;  /* bright green */
      --alert:#BC0000;   /* bright red */
      --muted:#3A3A3A;   /* dark grey */
      --pale:#FFFFE0;    /* soft highlight */
      --steel:#4682B4;   /* steel blue */
      --teal:#006737;    /* deep green-teal */

      /* Layout guards */
      --col-min: 420px;  /* minimum width for each column */
      color:var(--text);
      background:var(--bg);
      border:1px solid #d6e2d6;
      border-radius:18px;
      box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(22,35,31,0.08);
      overflow:hidden;
      font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Roboto,Arial,sans-serif;
    }

    .ai-header{
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--head),#16231F);
      color:#fff;
      padding:22px 24px;
      border-bottom:4px solid var(--accent);
    }
    .ai-header h2{ margin:0 0 6px 0; font-size:1.35rem; letter-spacing:.2px; }
    .ai-header p{ margin:0; opacity:.95; font-size:.98rem; }

    .ai-grid{
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(var(--col-min), 1fr));
      gap:18px;
      padding:18px;
    }

    .ai-panel{
      background:#f8fbf8;
      border:1px solid #d6e2d6;
      border-radius:14px;
      overflow:hidden;
      box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(22,35,31,0.06);
      min-width:0;
    }
    .ai-panel h3{
      margin:0;
      padding:14px 16px;
      font-size:1.05rem;
      color:#fff;
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--accent),#0e5a10);
      border-bottom:2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);
    }
    .ai-panel.alert h3{
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--alert),#8f0000);
    }

    .ai-list{ margin:0; padding:0; list-style:none; }
    .ai-item{
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;
      gap:12px;
      padding:14px 16px;
      border-bottom:1px solid rgba(32,52,46,0.06);
    }
    .ai-item:nth-child(odd){ background:var(--row-a); }
    .ai-item:nth-child(even){ background:var(--row-b); }

    /* Chips */
    .chip{
      display:inline-grid;
      place-items:center;
      width:38px; height:38px;
      border-radius:999px;
      color:#fff;
      font-weight:800;
      letter-spacing:.4px;
      box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(255,255,255,0.12),0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.12);
      user-select:none;
      flex:0 0 38px;
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--head),#0f1c18);
    }
    .chip.num{ background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--teal),#024c29); }
    .chip.warn{ background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--alert),#8f0000); }

    .ai-title{ margin:0 0 4px 0; font-weight:800; color:var(--head); }
    .ai-desc{ margin:0; font-size:.98rem; line-height:1.45; }

    .badge{
      display:inline-block; padding:2px 8px; border-radius:999px;
      font-size:.82rem; font-weight:700;
      background:var(--pale); color:var(--head);
      border:1px solid rgba(32,52,46,0.15);
      margin-left:6px;
    }
    .badge.alert{
      background:rgba(188,0,0,0.08); color:var(--alert); border-color:rgba(188,0,0,0.25);
    }

    .ai-foot{
      padding:14px 16px 18px 16px;
      background:#f4f7f4;
      border-top:1px dashed #d6e2d6;
      font-size:.95rem;
    }
    .ai-foot strong{ color:var(--head); }

    /* Hover effects (desktop) */
    @media (hover:hover){ .ai-item:hover{ filter:brightness(.98); } }

    /* Stack lists as &ldquo;cards&rdquo; on small screens (no layout collapse) */
    @media (max-width:520px){
      .ai-item{ grid-template-columns:1fr; }
    }</style>

  <div class="ai-header">
    <h2 id="acute-management-strategy">Acute Management Strategy</h2>
    <p>Immediate care steps, followed by red-flag warnings that require urgent medical attention.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="ai-grid">
    <!-- Column: Acute Management Strategy -->
    <section class="ai-panel" aria-label="Acute Management Strategy">
      <h3 id="strategy-first-aid">Strategy (First Aid)</h3>
      <ul class="ai-list">
        <li class="ai-item">
          <span class="chip num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ai-title">Immediate assessment</p>
            <p class="ai-desc">Use the <strong>OPQRST</strong> method to structure the pain history.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ai-item">
          <span class="chip num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ai-title">Apply PEACE protocol</p>
            <p class="ai-desc">For the first <strong>24&ndash;48 hours</strong> after soft-tissue injury.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ai-item">
          <span class="chip num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ai-title">Combine techniques</p>
            <p class="ai-desc"><strong>Cold therapy</strong> + <strong>elevation</strong> + <strong>compression</strong> to limit pain and swelling.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ai-item">
          <span class="chip num" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ai-title">Monitor circulation</p>
            <p class="ai-desc">Check capillary refill, skin colour, warmth, and sensation when using compression <span class="badge">Re-check regularly</span></p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ai-item">
          <span class="chip num" aria-hidden="true">5</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ai-title">Document response</p>
            <p class="ai-desc">Record pain levels (0&ndash;10) and treatment response to guide next steps.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ai-item">
          <span class="chip num" aria-hidden="true">6</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ai-title">Plan referral</p>
            <p class="ai-desc">Arrange appropriate <strong>GP/physio</strong> or urgent care based on severity and progress.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Column: Emergency Warning Signs -->
    <section class="ai-panel alert" aria-label="Warning Signs Requiring Emergency Medical Attention">
      <h3 id="warning-signs-seek-emergency-care">Warning Signs &ndash; Seek Emergency Care</h3>
      <ul class="ai-list">
        <li class="ai-item">
          <span class="chip warn" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ai-title">Severe, unrelenting pain</p>
            <p class="ai-desc">Pain that doesn&rsquo;t respond to initial first-aid measures.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ai-item">
          <span class="chip warn" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ai-title">Loss of sensation or movement</p>
            <p class="ai-desc">Numbness, tingling, weakness, or inability to move the limb.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ai-item">
          <span class="chip warn" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ai-title">Compromised circulation</p>
            <p class="ai-desc">Pale/blue skin, coldness, delayed capillary refill, or swelling that worsens.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ai-item">
          <span class="chip warn" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ai-title">Suspected fracture or dislocation</p>
            <p class="ai-desc">Deformity, crepitus, or bone end visibility&mdash;immobilise and seek urgent care.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ai-item">
          <span class="chip warn" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ai-title">Other concerning symptoms</p>
            <p class="ai-desc">E.g., chest pain, shortness of breath, fainting, fever, or signs of infection.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="ai-foot">
    <p><strong>Notes:</strong> If red-flag symptoms are present, call <strong>000</strong> or attend emergency care. Reassess regularly and update documentation after each intervention.</p>
  </div>
</div>
				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-734a3d1 external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="734a3d1" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="612" height="407" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/hot-pack.jpg" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1948964" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/hot-pack.jpg 612w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/hot-pack-300x200.jpg 300w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/hot-pack-600x400.jpg 600w" sizes="auto" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-7655451 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="7655451" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<h3 id="heat-vs-cold-for-pain-when-to-use-each"><b>Heat vs Cold for Pain: When to Use Each</b></h3><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Temperature therapy can be highly effective for pain management when applied appropriately. However, using the wrong type at the wrong time can worsen injuries and delay healing.</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-089cd16 external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="089cd16" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="936" height="468" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Cold-Therapy-Indications_-visual-selection.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1948945" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Cold-Therapy-Indications_-visual-selection.png 936w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/Cold-Therapy-Indications_-visual-selection-300x150.png.webp 300w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/Cold-Therapy-Indications_-visual-selection-768x384.png.webp 768w" sizes="auto" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-948f6b3 external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="948f6b3" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="900" height="468" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Heat-Therapy-Indications_-visual-selection.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1948949" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Heat-Therapy-Indications_-visual-selection.png 900w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/Heat-Therapy-Indications_-visual-selection-300x156.png.webp 300w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/Heat-Therapy-Indications_-visual-selection-768x399.png.webp 768w" sizes="auto" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-80861a0 external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="80861a0" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="800" height="650" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Temperature-Therapy-Safety_-visual-selection.png" class="attachment-large size-large wp-image-1948953" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Temperature-Therapy-Safety_-visual-selection.png 960w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/Temperature-Therapy-Safety_-visual-selection-300x244.png.webp 300w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/Temperature-Therapy-Safety_-visual-selection-768x624.png.webp 768w" sizes="auto" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-3790714 external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="3790714" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1594" height="984" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Penthrox.webp" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1948960" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Penthrox.webp 1594w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Penthrox-300x185.webp 300w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Penthrox-1024x632.webp 1024w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Penthrox-768x474.webp 768w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Penthrox-1536x948.webp 1536w" sizes="auto" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-79bfea0 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="79bfea0" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<h2 id="advanced-pain-management-in-first-aid-restricted-analgesics"><b>Advanced Pain Management in First Aid: Restricted Analgesics</b></h2><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Some <a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/course/hltaid014/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">first aid</a> situations may require advanced pain management techniques using restricted analgesics. These medications require special training, certification, and careful administration protocols.</span></p><h3 id="methoxyflurane-green-whistle-penthrox-overview"><b>Methoxyflurane Green Whistle (Penthrox) Overview</b></h3><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Methoxyflurane, commonly known as the &ldquo;green whistle,&rdquo; is an inhaled analgesic available to trained first aiders under specific circumstances. This medication provides rapid-onset pain relief for moderate to severe pain.</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-d20d7bf elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="d20d7bf" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p><b>PUAEME008 Provide Pain Management Requirements:</b></p><ul><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Nationally recognised training program</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Competency assessment in safe administration</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Understanding of indications and contraindications</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Knowledge of emergency protocols</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Regular skill maintenance and updates</span></li></ul><p><b>Methoxyflurane Characteristics:</b></p><ul><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Onset:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Pain relief within 2-3 minutes</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Duration:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Effective for 25-30 minutes per device</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Administration:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Self-administered under supervision</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Indications:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Moderate to severe pain from trauma</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Contraindications:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Respiratory depression, certain medical conditions</span></li></ul>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-1f60a39 external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="1f60a39" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="2560" height="1706" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Analgesic-Inhalation-System-scaled-1.webp" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1948968" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Analgesic-Inhalation-System-scaled-1.webp 2560w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Analgesic-Inhalation-System-scaled-1-300x200.webp 300w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Analgesic-Inhalation-System-scaled-1-1024x682.webp 1024w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Analgesic-Inhalation-System-scaled-1-768x512.webp 768w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Analgesic-Inhalation-System-scaled-1-1536x1024.webp 1536w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Analgesic-Inhalation-System-scaled-1-2048x1365.webp 2048w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Analgesic-Inhalation-System-scaled-1-600x400.webp 600w" sizes="auto" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-ee978fb elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="ee978fb" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<h3 id="entonox-analgesia-training-requirements"><b>Entonox Analgesia Training Requirements</b></h3><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Entonox (nitrous oxide/oxygen mix) represents another advanced pain management option requiring specialised training. This medication provides effective pain relief while maintaining patient consciousness and protective reflexes.</span></p><p><b>Training Components:</b></p><ul><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Physiological effects and mechanisms of action</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Proper equipment setup and maintenance</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Patient selection and contraindications</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Administration techniques and monitoring</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Emergency management and complications</span></li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Documentation and legal requirements</span></li></ul><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">First aiders interested in providing advanced pain management should consider pursuing additional qualifications through registered training organisations like <a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/course/puaeme008/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">First Aid Pro</a>, ensuring they meet all regulatory requirements and maintain appropriate insurance coverage.</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-a6d8f24 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="a6d8f24" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<h2 id="when-to-call-000-for-severe-pain-red-flag-symptoms"><b>When to Call 000 for Severe Pain: Red Flag Symptoms</b></h2><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Recognising when pain indicates a medical emergency requiring immediate ambulance response is crucial for preventing serious complications and ensuring appropriate patient outcomes.</span></p><h3 id="shock-and-severe-pain-first-aid-recognition">Shock and Severe Pain First Aid Recognition</h3><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Severe pain can trigger physiological shock responses that may be life-threatening. First aiders must recognise these signs and respond appropriately while managing the patient&rsquo;s pain.</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-744ed81 external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="744ed81" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="816" height="692" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Signs-of-Pain-Related-Shock_-visual-selection.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1948983" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Signs-of-Pain-Related-Shock_-visual-selection.png 816w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/Signs-of-Pain-Related-Shock_-visual-selection-300x254.png.webp 300w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/Signs-of-Pain-Related-Shock_-visual-selection-768x651.png.webp 768w" sizes="auto" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-5ca37ff external_elementor-repeater-item-none_external elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-image" data-id="5ca37ff" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="image.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
															<img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="672" height="1020" src="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Emergency-Management-Priorities_-visual-selection.png" class="attachment-large size-large wp-image-1948987" alt="" srcset="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Emergency-Management-Priorities_-visual-selection.png 672w, https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/wp-content/uploads/ees-webp/2025/11/Emergency-Management-Priorities_-visual-selection-198x300.png.webp 198w" sizes="auto" fetchpriority="low">															</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-db27d67 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="db27d67" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<h3 id="pain-relief-contraindications-first-aid-providers-must-know"><b>Pain Relief Contraindications First Aid Providers Must Know</b></h3><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Understanding when NOT to administer pain relief is as important as knowing when and how to provide it. Certain medical conditions, medications, and circumstances require alternative approaches or immediate medical referral.</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-af38afc elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="af38afc" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<!-- Contraindications for Pain Medications | Elementor/WordPress HTML Widget -->
<div class="contra-infographic" role="group" aria-label="Contraindications for Pain Medications">
  <style>.contra-infographic{
      /* Brand palette (same as above) */
      --bg:#FFFFFF;
      --row-a:#E4EAE4;     /* soft grey-green */
      --row-b:#DDEBE9;     /* soft mint/cyan */
      --text:#16231F;      /* very dark green */
      --head:#20342E;      /* dark green */
      --accent:#116914;    /* bright green */
      --alert:#BC0000;     /* bright red */
      --muted:#3A3A3A;     /* dark grey */
      --pale:#FFFFE0;      /* soft highlight */
      --steel:#4682B4;     /* steel blue */
      --teal:#006737;      /* deep green-teal */

      /* Layout guards */
      --col-min: 420px;    /* each column keeps this minimum width before stacking */

      color:var(--text);
      background:var(--bg);
      border:1px solid #d6e2d6;
      border-radius:18px;
      box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(22,35,31,0.08);
      overflow:hidden;
      font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Roboto,Arial,sans-serif;
    }

    /* Header */
    .ci-header{
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--head),#16231F);
      color:#fff;
      padding:22px 24px;
      border-bottom:4px solid var(--accent);
    }
    .ci-header h2{ margin:0 0 6px 0; font-size:1.35rem; letter-spacing:.2px; }
    .ci-header p{ margin:0; opacity:.95; font-size:.98rem; }

    /* Columns */
    .ci-grid{
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(var(--col-min), 1fr));
      gap:18px;
      padding:18px;
    }

    /* Panels */
    .ci-panel{
      background:#f8fbf8;
      border:1px solid #d6e2d6;
      border-radius:14px;
      overflow:hidden;
      box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(22,35,31,0.06);
      min-width:0;
    }
    .ci-panel h3{
      margin:0;
      padding:14px 16px;
      font-size:1.05rem;
      color:#fff;
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--steel),#315e80);
      border-bottom:2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);
    }
    .ci-panel.absolute h3{
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--alert),#8f0000);
    }
    .ci-panel.relative h3{
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--teal),#024c29);
    }

    /* Lists */
    .ci-list{ margin:0; padding:0; list-style:none; }
    .ci-item{
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;
      gap:12px;
      padding:14px 16px;
      border-bottom:1px solid rgba(32,52,46,0.06);
    }
    .ci-item:nth-child(odd){ background:var(--row-a); }
    .ci-item:nth-child(even){ background:var(--row-b); }

    /* Chips */
    .chip{
      display:inline-grid; place-items:center;
      width:38px; height:38px; border-radius:999px;
      color:#fff; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:.4px;
      box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(255,255,255,0.12),0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.12);
      user-select:none; flex:0 0 38px;
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--head),#0f1c18);
    }
    .chip.abs{ background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--alert),#8f0000); }
    .chip.rel{ background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--steel),#315e80); }

    .ci-title{ margin:0 0 4px 0; font-weight:800; color:var(--head); }
    .ci-desc{ margin:0; font-size:.98rem; line-height:1.45; }

    /* Badges */
    .badge{
      display:inline-block; padding:2px 8px; border-radius:999px;
      font-size:.82rem; font-weight:700;
      background:var(--pale); color:var(--head);
      border:1px solid rgba(32,52,46,0.15);
      margin-left:6px;
    }
    .badge.alert{
      background:rgba(188,0,0,0.08); color:var(--alert); border-color:rgba(188,0,0,0.25);
    }

    /* Footer */
    .ci-foot{
      padding:14px 16px 18px 16px;
      background:#f4f7f4;
      border-top:1px dashed #d6e2d6;
      font-size:.95rem;
    }
    .ci-foot strong{ color:var(--head); }

    /* Small screens */
    @media (max-width:520px){
      .ci-item{ grid-template-columns:1fr; }
    }

    /* Hover nicety (desktop) */
    @media (hover:hover){ .ci-item:hover{ filter:brightness(.98); } }</style>

  <div class="ci-header">
    <h2 id="contraindications-for-pain-medications">Contraindications for Pain Medications</h2>
    <p>Use this quick reference to identify when pain medicines should be avoided or used with caution in first aid.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="ci-grid">
    <!-- Absolute Contraindications -->
    <section class="ci-panel absolute" aria-label="Absolute Contraindications">
      <h3 id="absolute-contraindications">Absolute Contraindications</h3>
      <ul class="ci-list">
        <li class="ci-item">
          <span class="chip abs" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ci-title">Known allergies to specific medications</p>
            <p class="ci-desc">Do not administer if the person has a documented allergy or past severe reaction.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ci-item">
          <span class="chip abs" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ci-title">Unconscious patients (without advanced training)</p>
            <p class="ci-desc">No oral medications; manage airway/breathing and seek urgent help.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ci-item">
          <span class="chip abs" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ci-title">Suspected internal bleeding</p>
            <p class="ci-desc">Avoid <strong>NSAIDs</strong>; they may worsen bleeding risk&mdash;seek medical care promptly.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ci-item">
          <span class="chip abs" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ci-title">Severe respiratory depression</p>
            <p class="ci-desc">Urgent assessment required; monitor airway, breathing, circulation.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ci-item">
          <span class="chip abs" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ci-title">Signs of drug or alcohol intoxication</p>
            <p class="ci-desc">Avoid sedating/contraindicated medicines; prioritise safety and medical evaluation.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Relative Contraindications -->
    <section class="ci-panel relative" aria-label="Relative Contraindications Requiring Caution">
      <h3 id="relative-contraindications-use-with-caution">Relative Contraindications (Use with Caution)</h3>
      <ul class="ci-list">
        <li class="ci-item">
          <span class="chip rel" aria-hidden="true">&#9888;</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ci-title">Pregnancy</p>
            <p class="ci-desc">Especially when pregnancy status is unknown&mdash;seek pharmacist/GP advice.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ci-item">
          <span class="chip rel" aria-hidden="true">&#9888;</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ci-title">Chronic medical conditions</p>
            <p class="ci-desc">Kidney, liver, or heart disease can alter risk/benefit&mdash;check suitability first.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ci-item">
          <span class="chip rel" aria-hidden="true">&#9888;</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ci-title">Current prescription medications</p>
            <p class="ci-desc">Consider interactions and duplicate dosing with combination products.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ci-item">
          <span class="chip rel" aria-hidden="true">&#9888;</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ci-title">Age extremes</p>
            <p class="ci-desc">Very young or elderly may require adjusted doses/forms and closer monitoring.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ci-item">
          <span class="chip rel" aria-hidden="true">&#9888;</span>
          <div>
            <p class="ci-title">Uncertain diagnosis or mechanism</p>
            <p class="ci-desc">If the cause of pain is unclear, avoid masking symptoms&mdash;seek clinical advice.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="ci-foot">
    <p><strong>Notes:</strong> Follow product labels and local first aid protocols. When in doubt, consult a pharmacist/GP. For emergencies or red-flag symptoms, call <strong>000</strong>.</p>
  </div>
</div>
				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-8fa0776 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="8fa0776" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p><b>Master advanced pain management:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> First Aid Pro&rsquo;s <a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/course/puaeme008/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PUAEME008 training</a> covers restricted analgesics, legal requirements, and workplace safety protocols. Our experienced instructors provide hands-on training with the latest equipment and techniques.</span> <a href="https://www.firstaidpro.com.au/course/puaeme008/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Book your course</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> today and become qualified to provide advanced pain management in first aid.</span></p>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-4dc517d elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="4dc517d" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<!-- First Aid Pain Management &mdash; Knowledge Test Quiz (alignment-fixed) -->
<div id="fa-quiz-pain-01" class="firstaid-quiz" role="group" aria-label="First Aid Pain Management Quiz">
  <style>/* Scoped box-sizing + margin reset for consistent alignment */
    #fa-quiz-pain-01, #fa-quiz-pain-01 * , #fa-quiz-pain-01 *::before, #fa-quiz-pain-01 *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    #fa-quiz-pain-01 h1,#fa-quiz-pain-01 h2,#fa-quiz-pain-01 h3,#fa-quiz-pain-01 h4,#fa-quiz-pain-01 p { margin:0; }

    .firstaid-quiz{
      /* Brand palette */
      --bg:#FFFFFF;
      --row-a:#E4EAE4;    /* soft grey-green */
      --row-b:#DDEBE9;    /* soft mint/cyan */
      --text:#16231F;     /* very dark green */
      --head:#20342E;     /* dark green */
      --accent:#116914;   /* bright green */
      --accent-dark:#0e5a10;
      --alert:#BC0000;    /* bright red */
      --muted:#3A3A3A;    /* dark grey */
      --pale:#FFFFE0;     /* soft highlight */

      color:var(--text);
      background:var(--bg);
      border:1px solid #d6e2d6;
      border-radius:18px;
      box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(22,35,31,0.08);
      overflow:hidden;
      font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Roboto,Arial,sans-serif;
    }

    .fq-header{
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--head),#16231F);
      color:#fff;
      padding:22px 24px;
      border-bottom:4px solid var(--accent);
    }
    .fq-header h2{ font-size:1.35rem; letter-spacing:.2px; }
    .fq-header p{ opacity:.95; font-size:.98rem; margin-top:6px; }

    .fq-wrap{ padding:18px; }

    /* Score / actions bar */
    .fq-toolbar{
      display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:12px; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between;
      background:#f4f7f4; border:1px solid #d6e2d6; border-radius:12px; padding:12px 14px; margin-bottom:16px;
    }
    .fq-score{ font-weight:800; color:var(--head); }
    .fq-actions button{
      appearance:none; border:0; border-radius:10px; padding:10px 14px; cursor:pointer;
      font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.2px;
      box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(22,35,31,0.08);
    }
    .btn-check{ background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--accent),var(--accent-dark)); color:#fff; }
    .btn-reset{ background:#fff; color:var(--head); border:1px solid #d6e2d6; }
    .btn-check:disabled{ opacity:.6; cursor:not-allowed; }

    /* Question card */
    .fq-card{
      display:flex; flex-direction:column;
      background:#f8fbf8;
      border:1px solid #d6e2d6;
      border-radius:14px;
      overflow:hidden;
      box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(22,35,31,0.06);
      margin-bottom:16px;
      min-width:0;
    }
    .fq-card:nth-of-type(odd){ background:var(--row-a); }
    .fq-card:nth-of-type(even){ background:var(--row-b); }

    /* GREEN banners with strict grid for alignment */
    .fq-qhead{
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns: 34px 1fr;
      align-items:center;
      gap:10px;
      padding:14px 16px;
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--accent),var(--accent-dark));
      color:#fff;
      border-bottom:2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);
      line-height:1.3;
    }
    .fq-qhead .qnum{
      display:inline-grid; place-items:center; width:34px; height:34px; border-radius:999px;
      background:rgba(255,255,255,0.16); font-weight:800;
      box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(255,255,255,0.18);
    }
    .fq-qhead .qtext{ font-weight:600; }

    .fq-qbody{ padding:14px 16px; }

    fieldset{ border:0; margin:0; padding:0; }
    legend{ position:absolute; left:-9999px; }

    /* Options: strict 3-column grid = radio | letter | text */
    .fq-options{ display:grid; gap:10px; margin-top:10px; }
    .fq-option{
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns: 20px 28px 1fr;
      align-items:start;
      column-gap:10px;
      background:#fff;
      border:1px solid #d6e2d6; border-radius:10px; padding:10px 12px;
      transition:filter .2s, border-color .2s, box-shadow .2s;
    }
    .fq-option:hover{ filter:brightness(.98); }

    .fq-option input[type="radio"]{ width:18px; height:18px; margin:2px 0 0 0; }
    .opt-letter{ width:28px; text-align:center; font-weight:800; color:var(--head); }
    .opt-text{ line-height:1.45; }

    /* Feedback */
    .fq-feedback{
      margin-top:10px; padding:10px 12px; border-radius:10px; border:1px solid #d6e2d6; background:#fff;
      display:none;
    }
    .fq-feedback.correct{ display:block; border-color:rgba(17,105,20,0.35); background:#ecf6ee; color:var(--head); }
    .fq-feedback.incorrect{ display:block; border-color:rgba(188,0,0,0.35); background:#fdecec; color:#8f0000; }

    /* Marking states */
    .fq-option.correct{ border-color:rgba(17,105,20,0.6); box-shadow:0 0 0 3px rgba(17,105,20,0.12) inset; }
    .fq-option.incorrect{ border-color:rgba(188,0,0,0.6); box-shadow:0 0 0 3px rgba(188,0,0,0.12) inset; }

    @media (max-width:580px){
      .fq-toolbar{ flex-direction:column; align-items:flex-start; }
    }</style>

  <div class="fq-header">
    <h2 id="knowledge-test-quiz">Knowledge Test Quiz</h2>
    <p>Test your understanding of first aid pain management. Select one option for each question, then choose <strong>Check answers</strong>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="fq-wrap">
    <div class="fq-toolbar" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="fq-score">Score: <span class="score-val">0</span>/5</div>
      <div class="fq-actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn-check">Check answers</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-reset">Reset</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <form class="quiz-form" novalidate>
      <!-- Q1 -->
      <section class="fq-card" data-correct="b">
        <div class="fq-qhead">
          <span class="qnum">1</span>
          <span class="qtext">What does the &lsquo;P&rsquo; in OPQRST stand for, and why is it important?</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fq-qbody">
          <fieldset>
            <legend>Question 1</legend>
            <div class="fq-options">
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q1" value="a">
                <span class="opt-letter">a)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">Pressure &mdash; indicates injury severity</span>
              </label>
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q1" value="b">
                <span class="opt-letter">b)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">Provocation &mdash; identifies triggers that worsen or improve pain</span>
              </label>
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q1" value="c">
                <span class="opt-letter">c)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">Position &mdash; determines patient comfort</span>
              </label>
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q1" value="d">
                <span class="opt-letter">d)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">Prescription &mdash; checks medication history</span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </fieldset>
          <div class="fq-feedback" aria-live="polite" data-explain-correct="Correct. &lsquo;P&rsquo; is Provocation &mdash; it reveals what exacerbates or eases pain, guiding first aid decisions." data-explain-incorrect="Not quite. &lsquo;P&rsquo; stands for Provocation &mdash; understanding triggers helps tailor safe, effective care.">
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Q2 -->
      <section class="fq-card" data-correct="c">
        <div class="fq-qhead">
          <span class="qnum">2</span>
          <span class="qtext">When is cold therapy most appropriate for pain management?</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fq-qbody">
          <fieldset>
            <legend>Question 2</legend>
            <div class="fq-options">
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q2" value="a">
                <span class="opt-letter">a)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">Always when pain is present</span>
              </label>
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q2" value="b">
                <span class="opt-letter">b)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">Only for chronic conditions</span>
              </label>
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q2" value="c">
                <span class="opt-letter">c)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">Within the first 24&ndash;48 hours of an acute injury</span>
              </label>
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q2" value="d">
                <span class="opt-letter">d)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">After heat therapy has been tried</span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </fieldset>
          <div class="fq-feedback" aria-live="polite" data-explain-correct="Correct. Early cold therapy can help limit swelling and pain after acute injury." data-explain-incorrect="Not quite. It&rsquo;s generally most useful in the first 24&ndash;48 hours after an acute injury.">
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Q3 -->
      <section class="fq-card" data-correct="c">
        <div class="fq-qhead">
          <span class="qnum">3</span>
          <span class="qtext">What is the maximum daily dose of paracetamol for a healthy adult?</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fq-qbody">
          <fieldset>
            <legend>Question 3</legend>
            <div class="fq-options">
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q3" value="a">
                <span class="opt-letter">a)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">2000&nbsp;mg</span>
              </label>
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q3" value="b">
                <span class="opt-letter">b)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">3000&nbsp;mg</span>
              </label>
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q3" value="c">
                <span class="opt-letter">c)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">4000&nbsp;mg</span>
              </label>
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q3" value="d">
                <span class="opt-letter">d)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">5000&nbsp;mg</span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </fieldset>
          <div class="fq-feedback" aria-live="polite" data-explain-correct="Correct. Do not exceed 4,000&nbsp;mg in 24 hours for healthy adults." data-explain-incorrect="Not quite. The maximum for healthy adults is 4,000&nbsp;mg in 24 hours.">
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Q4 -->
      <section class="fq-card" data-correct="b">
        <div class="fq-qhead">
          <span class="qnum">4</span>
          <span class="qtext">Which condition is an absolute contraindication for ibuprofen?</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fq-qbody">
          <fieldset>
            <legend>Question 4</legend>
            <div class="fq-options">
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q4" value="a">
                <span class="opt-letter">a)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">Mild headache</span>
              </label>
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q4" value="b">
                <span class="opt-letter">b)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">History of stomach ulcers</span>
              </label>
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q4" value="c">
                <span class="opt-letter">c)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">Common cold</span>
              </label>
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q4" value="d">
                <span class="opt-letter">d)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">Muscle strain</span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </fieldset>
          <div class="fq-feedback" aria-live="polite" data-explain-correct="Correct. NSAIDs like ibuprofen are generally contraindicated with active or past peptic ulcer disease." data-explain-incorrect="Not quite. A history of stomach ulcers is a contraindication to ibuprofen use.">
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Q5 -->
      <section class="fq-card" data-correct="b">
        <div class="fq-qhead">
          <span class="qnum">5</span>
          <span class="qtext">When should you call 000 for a patient experiencing pain?</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fq-qbody">
          <fieldset>
            <legend>Question 5</legend>
            <div class="fq-options">
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q5" value="a">
                <span class="opt-letter">a)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">Only when pain level is 10/10</span>
              </label>
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q5" value="b">
                <span class="opt-letter">b)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">When pain is associated with altered consciousness or shock</span>
              </label>
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q5" value="c">
                <span class="opt-letter">c)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">Never; pain alone doesn&rsquo;t require emergency services</span>
              </label>
              <label class="fq-option">
                <input type="radio" name="q5" value="d">
                <span class="opt-letter">d)</span>
                <span class="opt-text">Only for children</span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </fieldset>
          <div class="fq-feedback" aria-live="polite" data-explain-correct="Correct. Red-flags like altered consciousness or shock warrant calling 000." data-explain-incorrect="Not quite. Call 000 when pain is accompanied by red-flag signs such as altered consciousness or shock.">
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </form>
  </div>

  <script defer src="data:text/javascript,%28function%28%29%7B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20quiz%20%3D%20document.getElementById%28%27fa-quiz-pain-01%27%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20if%28%21quiz%29%20return%3B%0D%0A%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20form%20%20%20%20%3D%20quiz.querySelector%28%27.quiz-form%27%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20checkBtn%3D%20quiz.querySelector%28%27.btn-check%27%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20resetBtn%3D%20quiz.querySelector%28%27.btn-reset%27%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20scoreEl%20%3D%20quiz.querySelector%28%27.score-val%27%29%3B%0D%0A%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20function%20clearMarks%28%29%7B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20opts%20%3D%20form.querySelectorAll%28%27.fq-option%27%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20for%28var%20i%3D0%3Bi%3Copts.length%3Bi%2B%2B%29%7B%20opts%5Bi%5D.classList.remove%28%27correct%27%2C%27incorrect%27%29%3B%20%7D%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20feeds%20%3D%20form.querySelectorAll%28%27.fq-feedback%27%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20for%28var%20j%3D0%3Bj%3Cfeeds.length%3Bj%2B%2B%29%7B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20feeds%5Bj%5D.classList.remove%28%27correct%27%2C%27incorrect%27%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20feeds%5Bj%5D.style.display%20%3D%20%27none%27%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20feeds%5Bj%5D.textContent%20%3D%20%27%27%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7D%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20radios%20%3D%20form.querySelectorAll%28%27input%5Btype%3D%22radio%22%5D%27%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20for%28var%20k%3D0%3Bk%3Cradios.length%3Bk%2B%2B%29%7B%20radios%5Bk%5D.disabled%20%3D%20false%3B%20%7D%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20scoreEl.textContent%20%3D%20%270%27%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20checkBtn.disabled%20%3D%20false%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%7D%0D%0A%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20function%20markQuiz%28%29%7B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20cards%20%3D%20form.querySelectorAll%28%27.fq-card%27%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20total%20%3D%20cards.length%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20correctCount%20%3D%200%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20firstUnanswered%20%3D%20null%3B%0D%0A%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20for%28var%20i%3D0%3Bi%3Ccards.length%3Bi%2B%2B%29%7B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20card%20%3D%20cards%5Bi%5D%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20correctVal%20%3D%20%28card.getAttribute%28%27data-correct%27%29%7C%7C%27%27%29.trim%28%29.toLowerCase%28%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20selected%20%3D%20card.querySelector%28%27input%5Btype%3D%22radio%22%5D%3Achecked%27%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20options%20%20%3D%20card.querySelectorAll%28%27.fq-option%27%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20feedback%20%3D%20card.querySelector%28%27.fq-feedback%27%29%3B%0D%0A%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20for%28var%20o%3D0%3Bo%3Coptions.length%3Bo%2B%2B%29%7B%20options%5Bo%5D.classList.remove%28%27correct%27%2C%27incorrect%27%29%3B%20%7D%0D%0A%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20if%28%21selected%29%7B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20if%28%21firstUnanswered%29%20firstUnanswered%20%3D%20card%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20feedback.classList.add%28%27incorrect%27%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20feedback.style.display%20%3D%20%27block%27%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20feedback.textContent%20%3D%20%27Please%20choose%20an%20option%20before%20checking.%27%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20continue%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7D%0D%0A%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20radios%20%3D%20card.querySelectorAll%28%27input%5Btype%3D%22radio%22%5D%27%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20for%28var%20r%3D0%3Br%3Cradios.length%3Br%2B%2B%29%7B%20radios%5Br%5D.disabled%20%3D%20true%3B%20%7D%0D%0A%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20chosen%20%3D%20%28selected.value%7C%7C%27%27%29.toLowerCase%28%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20chosenOpt%20%3D%20selected.closest%20%3F%20selected.closest%28%27.fq-option%27%29%20%3A%20selected.parentNode%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20correctOpt%20%3D%20null%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20for%28var%20p%3D0%3Bp%3Coptions.length%3Bp%2B%2B%29%7B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20var%20val%20%3D%20%28options%5Bp%5D.querySelector%28%27input%27%29%7C%7C%7B%7D%29.value%20%7C%7C%20%27%27%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20if%28val.toLowerCase%28%29%20%3D%3D%3D%20correctVal%29%7B%20correctOpt%20%3D%20options%5Bp%5D%3B%20break%3B%20%7D%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7D%0D%0A%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20if%28chosen%20%3D%3D%3D%20correctVal%29%7B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20correctCount%2B%2B%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20if%28chosenOpt%29%7B%20chosenOpt.classList.add%28%27correct%27%29%3B%20%7D%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20feedback.classList.remove%28%27incorrect%27%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20feedback.classList.add%28%27correct%27%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20feedback.style.display%20%3D%20%27block%27%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20feedback.textContent%20%3D%20feedback.getAttribute%28%27data-explain-correct%27%29%20%7C%7C%20%27Correct.%27%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7Delse%7B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20if%28chosenOpt%29%7B%20chosenOpt.classList.add%28%27incorrect%27%29%3B%20%7D%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20if%28correctOpt%29%7B%20correctOpt.classList.add%28%27correct%27%29%3B%20%7D%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20feedback.classList.remove%28%27correct%27%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20feedback.classList.add%28%27incorrect%27%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20feedback.style.display%20%3D%20%27block%27%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20feedback.textContent%20%3D%20feedback.getAttribute%28%27data-explain-incorrect%27%29%20%7C%7C%20%27Incorrect.%27%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7D%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7D%0D%0A%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20scoreEl.textContent%20%3D%20correctCount%20%2B%20%27%2F%27%20%2B%20total%3B%0D%0A%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20if%28firstUnanswered%29%7B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20firstUnanswered.scrollIntoView%28%7Bbehavior%3A%27smooth%27%2C%20block%3A%27center%27%7D%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7Delse%7B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20checkBtn.disabled%20%3D%20true%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%7D%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%7D%0D%0A%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20checkBtn.addEventListener%28%27click%27%2C%20markQuiz%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20resetBtn.addEventListener%28%27click%27%2C%20function%28%29%7B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20form.reset%28%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20clearMarks%28%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20quiz.scrollIntoView%28%7Bbehavior%3A%27smooth%27%2C%20block%3A%27start%27%7D%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%7D%29%3B%0D%0A%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20clearMarks%28%29%3B%0D%0A%20%20%20%20%7D%29%28%29%3B"></script>
</div>
