					<h3 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default" id="references">References
</h3>				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-ebdce68 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="ebdce68" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<ul><li><span style="font-weight: 400;">Better Health Channel. </span><a href="https://www.betterhealth.vic.gov.au/health/conditionsandtreatments/pain-and-pain-management-adults" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Pain Relief Medications</span></i></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">. Australian Government Department of Health.&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style="font-weight: 400;">Australian and New Zealand Committee on Resuscitation (ANZCOR). (2024). </span><a href="https://www.anzcor.org/home/first-aid-management-of-injuries" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">First Aid Guidelines</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span></a>&nbsp;</li><li><span style="font-weight: 400;">Better Health Channel. (2024). </span><a href="https://www.betterhealth.vic.gov.au/conditionsandtreatments/first-aid" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">First Aid and Emergency Care</span></i></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">. Victorian State Government.&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style="font-weight: 400;">Therapeutic Goods Administration (TGA). (2024). </span><a href="https://www.tga.gov.au/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods</span></i></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">. Australian Government Department of Health.&nbsp;</span></li><li><a href="https://training.gov.au/training/details/PUAEME008/unitdetails" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Training.gov.au. (2024). </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">PUAEME008 &ndash; Provide Pain Management</span></i></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">. Australian Government Department of Employment and Workplace Relations. </span></li><li><span style="font-weight: 400;">Dubois, B., &amp; Esculier, J. F. (2019). Soft-tissue injuries simply need PEACE and LOVE. </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">British Journal of Sports Medicine</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">, 54(2), 72-73.&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"><br></span></li><li><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14754753/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Bleakley, C., McDonough, S., &amp; MacAuley, D. (2004). The use of ice in the treatment of acute soft-tissue injury. </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">American Journal of Sports Medicine</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;">, 32(1), 251-261.</span></a>&nbsp;</li></ul>								</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-129650b elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="129650b" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h3 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default" id="frequently-asked-questions">Frequently Asked Questions</h3>				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-14c58af7 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-eael-adv-accordion" data-id="14c58af7" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="eael-adv-accordion.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					            <div class="eael-adv-accordion" id="eael-adv-accordion-14c58af7" data-scroll-on-click="no" data-scroll-speed="300" data-accordion-id="14c58af7" data-accordion-type="accordion" data-toogle-speed="300">
            <div class="eael-accordion-list">
					<div id="can-workplace-first-aiders-give-paracetamol-or-ibuprofen-to-employees" class="elementor-tab-title eael-accordion-header" tabindex="0" data-tab="1" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-3481"><span class="eael-advanced-accordion-icon-closed"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="fa-accordion-icon e-font-icon-svg e-fas-plus" viewbox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span><span class="eael-advanced-accordion-icon-opened"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="fa-accordion-icon e-font-icon-svg e-fas-minus" viewbox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span><span class="eael-accordion-tab-title">Can workplace first aiders give paracetamol or ibuprofen to employees?</span><svg aria-hidden="true" class="fa-toggle e-font-icon-svg e-fas-angle-right" viewbox="0 0 256 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M224.3 273l-136 136c-9.4 9.4-24.6 9.4-33.9 0l-22.6-22.6c-9.4-9.4-9.4-24.6 0-33.9l96.4-96.4-96.4-96.4c-9.4-9.4-9.4-24.6 0-33.9L54.3 103c9.4-9.4 24.6-9.4 33.9 0l136 136c9.5 9.4 9.5 24.6.1 34z"></path></svg></div><div id="elementor-tab-content-3481" class="eael-accordion-content clearfix" data-tab="1" aria-labelledby="can-workplace-first-aiders-give-paracetamol-or-ibuprofen-to-employees"><p><span style="font-weight: 400">Yes, trained first aiders can administer over-the-counter pain medications within their scope of practice. However, they must ensure the person has no contraindications, obtain consent, follow proper dosing guidelines, and maintain accurate records. Many workplaces require specific protocols for medication administration, so check your organisation&rsquo;s pain management in first aid procedures and ensure your first aid kit is fully stocked with appropriate medications.</span></p></div>
					</div><div class="eael-accordion-list">
					<div id="whats-the-difference-between-acute-and-chronic-pain-management-in-first-aid-situations" class="elementor-tab-title eael-accordion-header" tabindex="0" data-tab="2" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-3482"><span class="eael-advanced-accordion-icon-closed"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="fa-accordion-icon e-font-icon-svg e-fas-plus" viewbox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span><span class="eael-advanced-accordion-icon-opened"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="fa-accordion-icon e-font-icon-svg e-fas-minus" viewbox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span><span class="eael-accordion-tab-title">What's the difference between acute and chronic pain management in first aid situations?</span><svg aria-hidden="true" class="fa-toggle e-font-icon-svg e-fas-angle-right" viewbox="0 0 256 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M224.3 273l-136 136c-9.4 9.4-24.6 9.4-33.9 0l-22.6-22.6c-9.4-9.4-9.4-24.6 0-33.9l96.4-96.4-96.4-96.4c-9.4-9.4-9.4-24.6 0-33.9L54.3 103c9.4-9.4 24.6-9.4 33.9 0l136 136c9.5 9.4 9.5 24.6.1 34z"></path></svg></div><div id="elementor-tab-content-3482" class="eael-accordion-content clearfix" data-tab="2" aria-labelledby="whats-the-difference-between-acute-and-chronic-pain-management-in-first-aid-situations"><p><span style="font-weight: 400">Acute pain occurs suddenly due to injury or illness and typically requires immediate intervention with techniques like cold therapy, elevation, and appropriate medication. Chronic pain persists for weeks or months and usually requires ongoing medical management rather than first aid intervention. First aiders should focus on acute pain management while recognising that chronic conditions may affect how patients respond to treatment and may increase their risk of complications.</span></p></div>
					</div><div class="eael-accordion-list">
					<div id="when-should-i-call-an-ambulance-for-someone-experiencing-severe-pain" class="elementor-tab-title eael-accordion-header" tabindex="0" data-tab="3" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-3483"><span class="eael-advanced-accordion-icon-closed"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="fa-accordion-icon e-font-icon-svg e-fas-plus" viewbox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span><span class="eael-advanced-accordion-icon-opened"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="fa-accordion-icon e-font-icon-svg e-fas-minus" viewbox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span><span class="eael-accordion-tab-title">When should I call an ambulance for someone experiencing severe pain?</span><svg aria-hidden="true" class="fa-toggle e-font-icon-svg e-fas-angle-right" viewbox="0 0 256 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M224.3 273l-136 136c-9.4 9.4-24.6 9.4-33.9 0l-22.6-22.6c-9.4-9.4-9.4-24.6 0-33.9l96.4-96.4-96.4-96.4c-9.4-9.4-9.4-24.6 0-33.9L54.3 103c9.4-9.4 24.6-9.4 33.9 0l136 136c9.5 9.4 9.5 24.6.1 34z"></path></svg></div><div id="elementor-tab-content-3483" class="eael-accordion-content clearfix" data-tab="3" aria-labelledby="when-should-i-call-an-ambulance-for-someone-experiencing-severe-pain"><p><span style="font-weight: 400">&nbsp;Call 000 immediately if pain is associated with altered consciousness, signs of shock, difficulty breathing, chest pain, severe abdominal pain, suspected spinal injury, or if the person becomes unconscious. Also call if severe pain doesn&rsquo;t respond to appropriate first aid measures or if you&rsquo;re concerned about the person&rsquo;s overall condition. Remember that effective pain management in first aid situations can improve patient outcomes, but recognising when professional medical care is needed ensures the best possible results.</span></p></div>
					</div><div class="eael-accordion-list">
					<div id="how-do-i-manage-pain-in-someone-who-cant-take-standard-pain-medications" class="elementor-tab-title eael-accordion-header" tabindex="0" data-tab="4" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-3484"><span class="eael-advanced-accordion-icon-closed"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="fa-accordion-icon e-font-icon-svg e-fas-plus" viewbox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span><span class="eael-advanced-accordion-icon-opened"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="fa-accordion-icon e-font-icon-svg e-fas-minus" viewbox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span><span class="eael-accordion-tab-title">How do I manage pain in someone who can't take standard pain medications?</span><svg aria-hidden="true" class="fa-toggle e-font-icon-svg e-fas-angle-right" viewbox="0 0 256 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M224.3 273l-136 136c-9.4 9.4-24.6 9.4-33.9 0l-22.6-22.6c-9.4-9.4-9.4-24.6 0-33.9l96.4-96.4-96.4-96.4c-9.4-9.4-9.4-24.6 0-33.9L54.3 103c9.4-9.4 24.6-9.4 33.9 0l136 136c9.5 9.4 9.5 24.6.1 34z"></path></svg></div><div id="elementor-tab-content-3484" class="eael-accordion-content clearfix" data-tab="4" aria-labelledby="how-do-i-manage-pain-in-someone-who-cant-take-standard-pain-medications"><p><span style="font-weight: 400">&nbsp;Focus on non-pharmacological techniques such as cold therapy, positioning for comfort, elevation, gentle compression, and reassurance. These methods can be highly effective for pain relief without medication risks. Always consult with medical professionals about alternative approaches, and ensure you document the person&rsquo;s medication restrictions and any treatments provided. Consider that reducing the risk of further injury through proper immobilisation and support can significantly improve pain levels.</span></p></div>
					</div><div class="eael-accordion-list">
					<div id="what-should-bei-included-in-workplace-first-aid-training-regarding-pain-management" class="elementor-tab-title eael-accordion-header" tabindex="0" data-tab="5" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-3485"><span class="eael-advanced-accordion-icon-closed"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="fa-accordion-icon e-font-icon-svg e-fas-plus" viewbox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span><span class="eael-advanced-accordion-icon-opened"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="fa-accordion-icon e-font-icon-svg e-fas-minus" viewbox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span><span class="eael-accordion-tab-title">What should beI included in workplace first aid training regarding pain management?</span><svg aria-hidden="true" class="fa-toggle e-font-icon-svg e-fas-angle-right" viewbox="0 0 256 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M224.3 273l-136 136c-9.4 9.4-24.6 9.4-33.9 0l-22.6-22.6c-9.4-9.4-9.4-24.6 0-33.9l96.4-96.4-96.4-96.4c-9.4-9.4-9.4-24.6 0-33.9L54.3 103c9.4-9.4 24.6-9.4 33.9 0l136 136c9.5 9.4 9.5 24.6.1 34z"></path></svg></div><div id="elementor-tab-content-3485" class="eael-accordion-content clearfix" data-tab="5" aria-labelledby="what-should-bei-included-in-workplace-first-aid-training-regarding-pain-management"><p><span style="font-weight: 400">Workplace first aid training should cover pain assessment techniques, appropriate use of non-pharmacological interventions, safe administration of over-the-counter medications, recognition of medical emergencies, proper documentation, and understanding of when to access professional medical help. Training should also address specific workplace hazards and injury types common to your industry, ensuring first aiders can provide effective pain management while maintaining health and safety standards and reducing the likelihood of complications.</span></p></div>
					</div></div>				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-9dbc183 e-flex e-con-boxed elementor-repeater-item-default_padding elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover e-con e-parent" data-id="9dbc183" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container" data-settings='{"ang_container_spacing_size":"default_padding"}'>
					<div class="e-con-inner">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-137b9c7 elementor-repeater-item-none elementor-repeater-item-none_hover elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="137b9c7" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<script type="application/ld+json">
{
